# Beads Addendum — Holly Tracker Backend

This file is the adapter-specific reference for the **Beads** issue tracker
(`tracker = "beads"` in `.holly/config.toml`). Read alongside the universal
issue-tracker protocol in `src/holly/skills/issue-tracker/SKILL.md` (installed
as `.agents/skills/issue-tracker/SKILL.md`).

Beads provides persistent, dependency-aware task memory. Holly provides the
agent-facing command surface.

## Agent Rule

Agents use Holly for everything:

```bash
holly tracker ...
holly task ...
holly memory ...
holly chat ...
```

Do not call backend tracker, session, chat, memory, or process tools directly
for ordinary agent work. Holly wraps the adapter and owns lifecycle sequencing.

## Adapter Check

Run:

```bash
holly status
holly validate
```

This addendum applies when Holly reports `Adapter beads` or the project config
sets `adapter = "beads"`.

## Session Protocol

Find or create the work item:

```bash
holly tracker ready --limit 10
holly tracker show <issue-id>
holly tracker create "<title>" --type task --priority 2 --description "<context>"
```

Start the task:

```bash
eval "$(holly task start --id <issue-id> --intent '<agent-intent>')"
# read-only/non-implementation:
eval "$(holly task start --intent '<agent-intent>')"
```

The start command uses the inherited Holly session context, records the issue
ID or intent, and posts/verifies intent. With `--id`, it claims the issue,
creates or reuses the adapter worktree, and `cd`s there when eval'd. Without
`--id`, it records read-only intent and stays on the project root.
`HOLLY_SESSION_ID` is shell/runtime-owned and read-only; do not export,
generate, or overwrite it.

Record durable context:

```bash
holly tracker comment <issue-id> --message "<note>"
holly memory propose --text "<candidate memory>"
```

Finish the task:

```bash
eval "$(holly task finish)"
```

The finish command verifies committed work, lands it on the integration branch,
pushes it, closes the issue through the adapter, syncs tracker state, removes
the worktree, and clears task state.

## Issue Operations

Use these Holly commands:

```bash
holly tracker create "<title>" --type bug --priority 1 --description "<details>"
holly tracker update <issue-id> --status blocked
holly tracker comment <issue-id> --message "<context>"
holly tracker close <issue-id> --reason "Completed"
```

Use `--json` when another tool or script needs structured output.

## Recovery

Resume from Holly state:

```bash
holly task status
holly task resume
holly tracker show <issue-id>
```

If the hook blocks a write on the main checkout, run the exact Holly command it
prints. The expected start command is:

```bash
eval "$(holly task start {--id <issue-id> | --intent <agent-intent>})"
```

## Human / Adapter Notes

The Beads backend and Dolt sync are implementation details below the Holly CLI.
Humans maintaining the adapter may inspect backend tools for diagnosis, but
agent-facing guidance stays Holly-only.
